{"name":"Shaded Sun","hex":"#f3eba5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shaded","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being in the shade, not in direct light.","Having a slight colour added (of a diagram or picture) or being slightly darkened as if in the shade."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of shade"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shaded"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shading","blocks":[{"text":"Shading refers to the depiction of depth perception in 3D models or illustrations by varying the level of darkness. Shading tries to approximate local behavior of light on the object's surface and is not to be confused with techniques of adding shadows, such as shadow mapping or shadow volumes, which fall under global behavior of light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Flatshading01.png/330px-Flatshading01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shading"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"htt